        "turn_number": 3,
        "accepted_source_line": 42,
        "verbatim_accepted_section": "### Cool Hand turn 3, about 103–131 seconds\n\nThe opponent's turn draw and hand identities remain hidden except when cards are played. The complete action chain is:\n\n1. Cool Hand plays **Lucky Ice Pop** (`107-lucky-ice-pop-play.jpg`). It heals the 40-HP Bulbasaur to 60 HP (`110-lucky-ice-pop-heal-60hp.jpg`). The coin result is visibly **Heads**, so Lucky Ice Pop returns to the opponent's hand instead of being discarded (`113-lucky-ice-pop-heads.jpg`, `114-lucky-ice-pop-returned.jpg`).\n2. Cool Hand attaches one generated **Grass Energy** to Bulbasaur (`116-opponent-grass-attachment.jpg`).\n3. Cool Hand plays **Quick-Grow Extract** (`117-quick-grow-extract-play.jpg`). Its displayed text says to choose a Grass Pokémon in play and put a random Grass Pokémon from the deck that evolves from it onto it. The resulting animation evolves Bulbasaur into **Ivysaur** (`120-quick-grow-extract-evolves-ivysaur.jpg`). The new stable state is 100-HP Ivysaur, and the game explicitly reports that Ivysaur recovered from being Asleep (`121-ivysaur-evolution-clears-sleep.jpg`).\n4. Ivysaur's higher retreat cost now satisfies **Heavy Helmet**, whose “take 20 less damage” effect visibly activates (`123-heavy-helmet-effect-active.jpg`).\n5. Ivysaur uses **Synthesis**. Its readable attack text takes two Grass Energy from the Energy Zone and attaches them to Ivysaur (`127-ivysaur-synthesis.jpg`). The settled board shows three Grass Energy total: the ordinary attachment plus the two from Synthesis (`130-ivysaur-three-grass.jpg`). Synthesis deals no attack damage.\n\nEnd state: Cool Hand has lone Active Ivysaur at 100 HP, three Grass Energy, and an active Heavy Helmet; there is still no opposing Bench. The owner's board is unchanged: Swablu Active with one Psychic, Eevee with Small Balloon and Darkrai on the Bench. Score remains 0–0.",
